{"id": "unknown-2026-10-07-040", "date": "2026-10-07", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Colorado nature library draws on nature itself to power campus", "content": "<p>A library dedicated to helping people connect with nature is now drawing on nature itself to help power its mission. Namaste Solar has completed a rooftop solar installation at Anythink Nature Library, Colorado&#8217;s first public nature library, operated by Rangeview Library District. The 203.5-kW system is expected to generate about half of the facility&#8217;s electricity.&#8230;</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.solarpowerworldonline.com/2026/10/colorado-nature-library-draws-on-nature", "sources": [{"name": "solar_power_world", "url": "https://www.solarpowerworldonline.com/2026/10/colorado-nature-library-draws-on-nature-itself-to-power-campus/", "type": "rss"}]}
